# MTF Sniper Architecture-as-Code & Anti-AI-Slop Protocol

All changes touching `strategies/mtf_sniper/` are locked by the declarative `ArchitectureManifest` (`scripts/guardrails/manifest.py`) and enforced in real time via Cursor `postToolUse` hooks, Git `pre-commit`, and `docker/Dockerfile.custom`.

## 1. Strict Topological Layer DAG (`LINT003`, `LINT007–009`, `LINT020`, `LINT023`, `LINT030`)

Every layer may ONLY import from its explicit allowlist in `ArchitectureManifest.layer_allowed_imports` (applies to top-level, relative, and lazy function-level imports — **zero carve-outs**):

- `core/` → `{__root__, core}`
- `market/` → `{market}` (100% stateless indicators & numeric/safety masks)
- `signals/` → `{core, market, signals}` (**NEVER** imports `directional`, `execution`, `risk`, `intelligence`, `telemetry`, or `strategy_mtf_sniper`; concrete `*Sensor` classes inherit `BaseSensor` `LINT018` and never touch `enter_*`/`exit_*` `LINT021`)
- `directional/` → `{core, market, signals, directional}` (`long/` and `short/` stay strictly isolated `LINT003`; 1 Sub-System = 1 dedicated `DirectionalPolicyProtocol` class `LINT025` with distinct same-side `SetupRecipe.priority` `LINT024`)
- `telemetry/` → `{core, telemetry}`
- `risk/` → `{core, risk}`
- `intelligence/` → `{__root__, core, directional, intelligence}`
- `execution/` → `{core, market, signals, directional, execution}` (`EntryPipeline` MUST route all signals through `SetupComposer.compose_suite(...)` `LINT026`/`LINT029`)
- `strategy_mtf_sniper.py` (Facade) → `{__root__, core, market, execution, intelligence, risk, telemetry}` (**NEVER** imports `signals`, `directional`, `talib`, or `technical` directly `LINT017`/`LINT030`)

## 2. Anti-AI-Slop Code Hygiene (`LINT001–002`, `LINT011–016`, `LINT031–036`)

- **`LINT031` (Topology & Anti-Sprawl):** Never create unapproved subdirectories (`utils/`, `helpers/`, `common/`, `v2/`, `tmp/`), duplicate/slop filenames (`*_v2.py`, `*_new.py`, `*_old.py`, `*_tmp.py`, `*helper*.py`, `*util*.py`), or `.md` files outside `docs/`.
- **`LINT032` (No Placeholders or Stubs):** No `TODO`/`TBD`/`XXX`/`PLACEHOLDER` comments (`LINT001` also bans `workaround`/`hack`/`fixme`), and no concrete `pass` / `...` / `NotImplementedError` method bodies outside `ABC`/`Protocol`.
- **`LINT033` (No Blanket Suppressions):** Never write bare `# type: ignore` (must specify `[error-code]`), bare `# noqa` (must specify `: RULE_ID`), `eval()`, or `exec()`.
- **`LINT034` (Hot-Path & Logging Hygiene):** Never call `print()` in strategy code (use `logger.*`), and never iterate DataFrames row-by-row with `.iterrows()`, `.itertuples()`, or `.apply(..., axis=1)`.
- **`LINT035` (Size & Mutability Budgets):** Subsystem modules `<= 550` LOC, functions `<= 165` LOC, McCabe complexity `<= 12` (`LINT019`), comment density `<= 5.0%` (`LINT002`), 100% English in Python (`LINT012`), no mutable default arguments (`=[]`, `={}`).
- **`LINT036` (Docs-to-Code Sync):** Keep `docs/{ARCHITECTURE,DATA_CONTRACTS,PHILOSOPHY}.md` synced with `STRATEGY_VERSION`, `SensorType` values, and active class names.

## 3. Mandatory Verification CLI

```bash
.venv/bin/python scripts/lint_guardrails.py --verify-all
```
